# oracle: pair hippo on the HIPPO water hexamer (examples/amoeba: data.water_hexamer.hippo, hippo_water.prm and hippo_water.key: cutoff 10, taper 8, polar-eps 1e-5, usolve-diag 1.0; bond_style class2, angle_style amoeba, boundary s s s, one/five special bonds). The Pauli repulsion (c_p[2]), the damped dispersion (c_p[3]), the charge-penetration multipoles (c_p[4]), the induced-dipole polarization (c_p[5], pe) and the charge transfer (c_p[6]) energies and the forces at step 0 and after 10 NVE steps.
# oracle-inputs: w119amoeba_hippo_hexamer.data w119amoeba_hippo_water.prm w119amoeba_hippo.key
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 skip=press,c_virial[1],c_virial[2],c_virial[3],c_virial[4],c_virial[5],c_virial[6]
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): the engine agrees with native to 2.8e-14 relative in pe, 6.6e-15 in c_p[2], 2.1e-14 in c_p[4], 2.8e-15 in c_p[5] and the forces after 10 steps to 4.7e-12 relative.
units           real
boundary        s s s
atom_style      amoeba
bond_style      class2
angle_style     amoeba
dihedral_style  none
fix             amtype all property/atom i_amtype ghost yes
fix             extra all property/atom i_amgroup d_redID d_pval ghost yes
fix             extra2 all property/atom i_polaxe d2_xyzaxis 3
read_data       w119amoeba_hippo_hexamer.data fix amtype NULL "Tinker Types"
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.5 0.5 0.5 one/five yes
pair_style      hippo
pair_coeff      * * w119amoeba_hippo_water.prm w119amoeba_hippo.key
compute         p all pair hippo
compute         virial all pressure NULL virial
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl c_p[1] c_p[2] c_p[3] c_p[4] c_p[5] c_p[6] press c_virial[1] c_virial[2] c_virial[3] c_virial[4] c_virial[5] c_virial[6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
fix             1 all nve
thermo          10
run             0
run             10
